{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges and their identity.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists every edge once (each copy of a parallel edge, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each self-loop, once), and an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its identity. The edge is reached","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from both its endpoints through ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", always at that one position, so a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keyed by ","type":"text"},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a weight) is the same in both directions. Positions are valid until the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is mutated.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counting."}]},{"text":" Neighborhoods count edge ends. A vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"w ≠ v"},{"text":" appears in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once per edge between them. A self-loop has both its ends at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" appears in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"text":" twice per loop, and the loop’s position twice in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacency_list"},{"text":", LEMON, igraph). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of:)"},{"text":" is the length of either, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop counts 2 and the degrees sum to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex and edge indices."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives adjacency in index space. A representation with dense edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices also reports "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps edge positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-to-one onto "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_index"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":"), so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them parallel to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Laws.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every conformer satisfies:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"vertexCount == vertices.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices; "},{"code":"edgeCount == edges.count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" as an endpoint;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oppositeVertex(to: v, acrossEdgeAt: e)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e].oppositeVertex(to: v)"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the opposite vertices in the same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The degrees sum to ","type":"text"},{"code":"2 * edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true exactly for the edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in either orientation, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Asking again gives the same answer."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index order: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":"th vertex."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapped through "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt: e)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e]"},{"type":"text","text":"’s ends mapped through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With edge indices, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndexBound == edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is one-to-one onto","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and, with vertex indices too,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mapped through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in the same order.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With edge indices, "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in index order: the "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"th position of "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has "},{"code":"edgeIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". So an algorithm that gathers edges from the index-space rows can order them by position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a tie rule) without walking "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", members with default implementations are requirements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a representation’s faster version is the one generic code calls, and a wrapper must forward"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has no mutation; mutation belongs to concrete types. It does not refine","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{